 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, you are about to draw 2 cards at random (without replacement) from a deck containing only these 10 cards: <span data-math=\"{\\text{A}}♡\">{\\text{A}}♡</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{A}}♠\">{\\text{A}}♠</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{A}}♣\">{\\text{A}}♣</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{A}}\\diamondsuit\">{\\text{A}}\\diamondsuit</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{K}}♠\">{\\text{K}}♠</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{K}}♣\">{\\text{K}}♣</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{Q}}♡\">{\\text{Q}}♡</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{Q}}♠\">{\\text{Q}}♠</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{J}}♡\">{\\text{J}}♡</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{J}}♠\">{\\text{J}}♠</span>.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 516701,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the probability of drawing 2 aces?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample space:</p> \n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A heart</td>\n<td>A spade</td>\n<td>A club</td>\n<td>A diamond</td>\n<td>K spade</td>\n<td>K club</td>\n<td>Q heart</td>\n<td>Q spade</td>\n<td>J heart</td>\n<td>J spade</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>For the first card, you have 4 Aces out of 10 cards.</p>\n<p>For the second card, you have 3 Aces and 9 cards.</p>\n<p>The Multiplication Rule for Probability: If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are events associated with the first and second stages of an experiment, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{and}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ P}}\\left( {F|E} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(Ace, Ace) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{{10}}\\left( {\\frac{3}{9}} \\right) = \\frac{{12}}{{90}} = \\frac{2}{{15}}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{{15}}\">\\frac{2}{{15}}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 516702,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the probability of drawing an ace first and a king second?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample space:</p> \n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A heart</td>\n<td>A spade</td>\n<td>A club</td>\n<td>A diamond</td>\n<td>K spade</td>\n<td>K club</td>\n<td>Q heart</td>\n<td>Q spade</td>\n<td>J heart</td>\n<td>J spade</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>For the first card, you have 4 Aces out of 10 cards.</p>\n<p>For the second card, you have 2 kings and 9 cards.</p>\n<p>The Multiplication Rule for Probability: If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are events associated with the first and second stages of an experiment, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{and}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ P}}\\left( {F|E} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(Ace, Ace) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{{10}}\\left( {\\frac{2}{9}} \\right) = \\frac{8}{{90}} = \\frac{4}{{45}}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{{45}}\">\\frac{4}{{45}}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
